# Optimizer facade.
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:optimize" privata optimize
#
# PML0-U3 ledger disposition (pml0-proof-api-ledger.md, gradus 33df687) —
# executed at PML1-U6: RETIRE sgd_step_2x2 (ledger row 10) and sgd_step_4x4
# (row 11). Neither had a live caller anywhere in the container (grep-
# verified); the same update math (param − lr·grad) is inlined in the
# caller-backed steppers train_step_2x2 / train_step_4x4 (src/train.fab,
# ledger rows 16-17, admitted). The FMIR stepper's library→library call gap
# (recorded in src/train.fab) is why the duplication exists; it does not
# convert "no caller" into a caller, so the clean-break rule retires the
# standalone symbols. The inlined copies in src/train.fab are the surviving
# surface.
#
# This module is now an empty facade (like src/data.fab) until PML4 lands
# optimizers on the production parameter surface.
#
# Architectural rule: optimizers consume raw parameter tensors and gradient
# tensors. They do not know about layer abstractions or architectures. This
# module must not import from gradus:nn, gradus:attention, or
# gradus:transformer. No module owns a backend or device handle.
